## 9. Safety

This project is intended for educational and research purposes.

Testing should be conducted only in an authorized, isolated laboratory.
Firewall enforcement can interrupt network connectivity. Keep
enforcement in dry-run mode until end-to-end detection, decision logic,
source-address validation, and rollback procedures have been
thoroughly tested.

Do not remove or overwrite existing firewall rules without verifying
their purpose and having a recovery plan.

## 10. Current Project Status

The ML evaluation, decision engine, and controlled Phase 6 dry-run
integration have been verified.

Remaining work includes validating detection with controlled attack
traffic, evaluating false-positive and false-negative behavior in
the live environment, confirming the full intended dual-layer
architecture, and completing final documentation and demonstrations.

RESOLUTE remains a research prototype; its reported dataset metrics
should not be interpreted as proof of production readiness.
